\caption{Per-type effect sizes ($\Delta$pp) with Newcombe 95\% CIs. Types form a partial ordering: incompleteness as upper bound (conditional on information-addition confound), coreferential as lower bound, and a mid-range equivalence cluster. Mid-tier ordering is margin-dependent (\S\ref{sec:results}).}
\label{fig:forest_plot}
\end{figure}

\begin{figure}[t]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=\columnwidth]{figures/fig3_heatmap.pdf}
\caption{Violation rates (\%) by model and type under ambiguous conditions ($n = 2{,}997$). Authorization scope varies 52\,pp across models ($\kappa = 0.385$), reflecting differential safety training; incompleteness remains uniformly high (46--62\%). C4 interaction is authorization-scope-specific (\S\ref{sec:c4}).}
\label{fig:heatmap}
\end{figure}

\label{sec:c4}C4 (model$\times$type interaction) is exploratory. The interaction is driven entirely by authorization scope (Claude 12\% vs.\ GPT-5.4/DeepSeek $>$60\%; Figure~\ref{fig:heatmap}); excluding it, the interaction vanishes ($p = 0.97$; Appendix~\ref{app:c4_sans_auth}). Cross-judge validation confirms model rankings (Fleiss' $\kappa = 0.717$; Appendix~\ref{app:cross_judge}).

\section*{Limitations}
\label{sec:limitations}

Our ambiguity pairs are synthetically constructed, so the 34.0\,pp effect is an upper bound; the SOPBench replication ($+$12.7\,pp) provides a cross-benchmark lower bound. We evaluate seven API-accessible models across two customer-service domains at temperature $= 0$; other domains, smaller models, and stochastic sampling remain untested. Failure mode coding relies on LLM annotators ($\kappa = 0.52$; human $\kappa = 0.15$, rising to $0.34$--$0.52$ after collapsing the spurious-compliance/structural-misparse boundary), though the coder prompt excludes ambiguity type labels, preventing type--mechanism contamination. At temperature $> 0$, stochastic sampling would likely increase variance in both conditions but is unlikely to eliminate the directional effect, given its magnitude ($+$31.0\,pp excluding incompleteness) and cross-model consistency.

\section*{Data and Code Availability}
The 300 clause pairs, evaluation pipeline, analysis scripts, and raw episode traces will be released upon publication at \url{https://github.com/anonymous/policy-ambiguity-safety}.

